description: Prevent accidental loss of git history, migrations, DB, and secrets
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git and data safety

- Do not `git push --force`, `git reset --hard`, or `git clean -fd` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not delete or rewrite `prisma/migrations/`.
- Do not drop/truncate production Postgres or delete the Prisma project.
- Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, API keys, or connection strings.
- Push finished work so it is not only on one machine.

## Where data lives

- Code + seed + migrations → GitHub
- Watches / users / sessions → Prisma Postgres (not git)
- Secrets → Vercel env + `.env.local` only; keep `.env.example` as key names only
